WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday!

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.540
I was gonna make a thoughts from places video from Dublin,

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.300
but then I realized that you took all of my footage

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.280
and used it in your Dublin video,

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:14.680
so I'm left with just this clip of a woman smelling her pitted shame

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.360
like she is an opponent of the Swintown Swoodilipopers.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.760
Who, by the way, Hank, have three games left

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.840
in their entire FIFA '11 history and are on the cusp of winning the Barclay's Premier League.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.480
Link in the doobly-doo.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.600
So Hank, I was pretty upset with you for borrowing all of my footage from Dublin,

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.480
But then something much more important happened.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.200
I began to develop a cold sore.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.420
You can't really see it, but you know how you know you're gonna get one before you get one,

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:35.980
yeah, I know I'm gonna get one.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.480
So, Hank, why is that such a big deal?

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.660
Well, on Thursday, I'm gonna be in a Google Plus Hangout with

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.900
the President of the United States, Barack Obama,

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.080
and I am probably going to have a cold sore.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.860
My only hope of not having a cold sore is this stuff,

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.600
Abreva, which is the only FDA approved medication for cold sores,

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:54.100
and literally costs more than gold.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.140
Wait, did you just say I was going to be in a Google Plus Hangout

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.600
with the president of the United States of America?

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.820
[Makes a siren sound]

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.600
Is the sound that my anxiety makes.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.960
Hank, I have no idea why this happened,

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.400
but someone at Google called me a couple of days ago

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.640
and was like, "Do you want to hang out with the President?"

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.600
And I was like, "Neee, it depends.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:12.980
The president of what?"

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:14.660
Because I just hung out with the president of DFTBA Records,

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.720
Hank Green, for like a week and a half,

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.120
and he was like alright, but you know, I wouldn't do it again.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.880
And they were like, "Yeah, the President of the United States,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.500
Barack Obama. Do you want to be in a Google Hangout and ask him a few questions?"

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:26.340
And I was like, "Mmm...okay.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.220
So, Hank, I am gonna get to ask the President some questions.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.300
I'm gonna improvise a bit, but I have prepared a few.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.420
My first question is, "H-hi Mr. President, my name is John Green,

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:34.880
OH MY GOD WHAT IS AIR?!"

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.840
Then I also have, "Would you rather fight ten duck-size horses

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:39.660
or one horse-size duck?"

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:43.380
And of course, "Mr. President, I can't help but notice that Canada got rid of its one cent coin,

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:45.440
and nothing bad happened. HOW DO WE STILL LIVE IN A WORLD WITH PENNIES?!"

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.160
And of course, I have to ask him who the eff is Hank.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.540
By the way, Hank, you can also ask questions to the President, as can anyone.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.960
There's a link in the doobly-doo to submit your questions.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:56.820
There is also a link in the doobly-doo to RSVP to the Hangout, or whatever,

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.060
I don't understand this terminology.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.520
But basically, it will be live on YouTube at 4:50 PM Eastern Time on Thursday,

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.760
I would be the one with the cold sore.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.220
Anyway, Hank, I'm intellectually aware of the fact the President of the United States doesn't care if I have a cold sore,

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.480
and also, that he will forget who I am,

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:12.580
within like 4 seconds at the end of the Google Hangout,

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:15.560
so that he can go back to like...country running.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.960
But I am none the less extremelly anxious of the cold sore,

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:20.240
and also every other facet of this interaction.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.860
And I saw a similar phenomenon, albiet on a much different scale, when we were on tour,

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:28.020
because many people, when we met them, were very, like, nervous and self-conscious.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.400
Hank, we met more than 6,000 Nerdfighters in ten days,

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:34.520
and I can say with authority that NONE of them had anything to be embarrassed about.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.640
But I know that many of them still felt embarrassed anyway.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.340
I also felt embarrassed.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.380
And that's kinda the inherent problem with meeting people you admire or whose work you really like,

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:47.960
it will never be 'normal' because you're always going to be hyper-conscious of everything that could go wrong.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:53.520
And if, say, you're President of the United States, you have those interactions with people EVERY SINGLE DAY, Hank.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.560
Like, most of your interactions, even with your staff or with people who are like,

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.460
"Oh my God, that's the President, everybody be calm."

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:01.000
THAT is the number one reason why I would never wanna be President.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:04.320
The number two reason is that no matter how sensible your policy idea is,

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.780
people only want to talk about ideology.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.920
And the number three reason is that I get cold sores every winter, and if you're President,

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.260
you can't hide.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:13.880
Hank, when the Yeti and I started dating, she told me that when she was in 8th grade,

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:19.860
she realized that everyone else was thinking about themselves as much as she was thinking about herself,

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.840
and that therefore, no one else had any time to think about her.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:26.940
This epiphany was one of the central reasons why Sarah was a relatively well-adjusted teenager.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:30.060
She realized that when she was like, thirteen,

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.660
I realized it when I...I'm actually still trying to internalize it.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:34.480
Hopefully it will happen before Thursday afternoon.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.440
But regardless Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

